@node Requirements
@chapter Requirements

@cindex Requirements


@itemize
@item
macOS 15.7 (Sequoia) +
@item
GNU Emacs 30.1+
@item
Safari 26+
@item
Python 3+
@end itemize

While not strictly required@comma{} no configuration is required if Scrim is installed.

@itemize
@item
@uref{http://yummymelon.com/scrim/, Scrim} v1.0+
@end itemize

@node Install
@chapter Install

@cindex Install


Install the iCloud Shortcut by clicking the link below:

@itemize
@item
@uref{https://www.icloud.com/shortcuts/dee5783c765443dd8c231b2cc44f8e94, Open in Emacs Info Shortcut}
@end itemize

If you have @uref{http://yummymelon.com/scrim/, Scrim} installed@comma{} you are ready to go.

Alternately you can edit the Shortcut to use @code{emacsclient}. This requires you to set the following variables in the Python script accordingly:

@example
use_scrim = False
# Set to your local configuration if use_scrim = False
emacsclient_path = "<path to emacsclient>"
@end example

@node Usage
@chapter Usage

@enumerate
@item
From Safari@comma{} open a web page generated via Texinfo HTML export.

@item
From the main menu bar@comma{} click on the Shortcuts icon and choose the menu item ``Open in Emacs Info''.
@end enumerate


@image{images/counterpart-shortcuts-menu,,,,png}



@enumerate
@item
The counterpart Info node of the web page should be displayed in Emacs Info.
@end enumerate

